# AI working state

Globally-useful state only. Detail lives in `state/<track>.md` — see the
index below. Read this file first every session; read a track's state file
only when you are touching that track.

## Latest

`internal/broadcast`: the fan-out primitive, now with two implementations
behind one interface. `MapChan` (map behind an RWMutex, buffered channel
per subscriber) is the reference; `Ring` (one shared ring buffer, each
subscriber reading at its own position) is the one to build on. Ring's
Broadcast is O(1) in the subscriber count — 8ns flat against MapChan's
48ns to 706us — and at an honest ~100% delivery it costs 17.7 ns/msg at a
thousand subscribers against 98.7, roughly flat where MapChan's
quadruples. Receiving became batch-oriented to make that possible. Full
detail, baselines and the harness traps are in `state/broadcast.md`.
Nothing consumes the package yet — the next milestone is still the walking
skeleton (config + HTTP server + `/ws` upgrade + read/write pumps + an
`httptest`-based client test).

